    "termsOfAccess": "Dear user, \r\n\r\nYou are welcome to download the materials of the Dataverse folder entitled “Autonomy deficits as vulnerability for anxiety: Evidence from two laboratory-based studies”, provided you agree with the following conditions: \r\n\r\n1. The downloader undertakes to keep confidential any information in the present data concerning individual persons, households, enterprises or institutions which comes to his/her knowledge during the work on the data. \r\n\r\n2. He/she undertakes not to distribute data to others without written permission from L. E. Kunst. \r\n\r\n3. He/she undertakes to use the present data for purely scientific (i.e. non-commercial) research only. \r\n\r\n4. He/she contacts at least one of the (co-)authors of the Anxiety, Stress, & Coping article, in case he/she want to publish or report on these dataset(s). If appropriate, he/she agrees to include a member of this research group as co-author. \r\n\r\n5. He/she includes the following acknowledgement in any publication based on the present dataset(s): In this paper use is made of data of Kunst et al. (2019), including the Anxiety, Stress & Coping reference: L. E. Kunst, J. Maas, M. A. L. M. Van Assen, W. Van der Heijden & M. H. J. Bekker (2019) Autonomy deficits as vulnerability for anxiety: Evidence from two laboratory-based studies, Anxiety, Stress & Coping, DOI: 10.1080/10615806.2019.1580697\r\n\r\n6. Downloading the materials does not grant exclusivity on the data or the subject. In the situation when proposals with a comparable subject will be submitted, agreement will be sought between the different parties. \r\n\r\n7. This statement shall remain valid, even after conclusion of the work of the present data. \r\n\r\n",
